  "learn.act.password": "Defensive Checklist & Hands-On Practice:\n\n1. The 4-Word Passphrase Method:\nCreate a memorable passphrase combining 4 random, unrelated Amharic or English words (e.g., 'bunna-mesob-ansole-dembel'). It takes centuries to brute-force yet requires zero stressful memorization.\n\n2. Switch to TOTP Authenticator Apps:\nEnable Google Authenticator, Aegis, or Bitwarden on your Google, Telegram, and social media accounts. This stops SIM swap attacks from compromising your logins.\n\n3. Enable Telegram Two-Step Cloud Password:\nGo to Telegram Settings > Privacy and Security > Two-Step Verification. Set a strong secondary password with an encrypted hint.\n\n4. Practice in ABBAY CYBERGUARD M2 Hardening Lab:\nAudit your stored credentials, calculate their entropy score, and generate hardened offline passwords safely.",
  "learn.act.phishing": "Defensive Checklist & Hands-On Practice:\n\n1. The 5-Second Pause Rule:\nNever click links in unexpected messages. Pause and ask: Did I request this notification? Is the sender verified?\n\n2. Safe Domain Inspection Drill:\nOn desktop, hover your mouse over the link to preview the destination URL. On mobile, long-press the link to inspect without opening. Use ABBAY CYBERGUARD M1 Threat Checker to safely scan suspicious URLs.\n\n3. Out-of-Band Channel Verification:\nIf a message claims your bank account is locked, open your official mobile banking app directly or call customer support (Ethio Telecom 994, Telebirr 127, CBE 951) using numbers you already know.\n\n4. Emergency Containment Steps:\nIf you inadvertently tapped a suspicious link or entered credentials:\n- Immediately disconnect your mobile device from mobile data and Wi-Fi.\n- Call your bank or mobile money operator to freeze the affected wallet immediately.\n- Change passwords from a separate, secure device.\n- Document the message and capture screenshots to prepare an M3 Incident Report.",
  "learn.act.privacy": "Defensive Checklist & Hands-On Practice:\n\n1. Conduct a Personal Privacy Audit:\nSearch your full name and phone number on Google and Telegram. Request removal or adjust privacy settings for any publicly exposed documents.\n\n2. Lockdown Telegram & Social Settings:\n- In Telegram: Go to Settings > Privacy and Security. Set 'Phone Number' to 'Nobody' and 'Calls' to 'My Contacts'.\n- In Facebook: Lock your profile, restrict past posts to friends only, and hide your friend list from public view.\n\n3. The Out-of-Band Verification Rule:\nWhenever a friend or colleague asks for money or verification codes over chat, call them directly over cellular voice to confirm their identity before taking action.\n\n4. Redact Documents Before Sending:\nNever send unredacted ID cards. Blur National ID numbers, Kebele stamps, and birth dates unless communicating with a legally verified institution.",
  "learn.act.response": "Emergency 15-Minute Containment Checklist:\n\n1. Step 1: Network Isolation\nImmediately disconnect the affected phone or computer from Wi-Fi and mobile data. Unplug the Ethernet cable. Do NOT turn off the computer if volatile memory analysis is needed.\n\n2. Step 2: Emergency Financial Freeze\nCall Ethio Telecom (994), Telebirr (127), or your bank's emergency customer service immediately from another phone. Request an immediate temporary account freeze.\n\n3. Step 3: Revoke Active Sessions\nFrom a clean, secondary device, log into your email, Google, and Telegram accounts. Navigate to Settings > Devices / Security and click 'Terminate All Other Sessions'. Then immediately change passwords.\n\n4. Step 4: Preserve Digital Evidence\n- Take high-resolution photos of screens showing transaction IDs, fraud messages, and timestamps.\n- Do NOT delete fraudulent SMS or chat threads—they contain critical metadata.\n\n5. Step 5: Draft an M3 Incident Report\nUse ABBAY CYBERGUARD M3 Incident Response to format a structured, privacy-safe report ready for submission to INSA (Ethio-CERT) or local cybercrime investigators.",
  "learn.act.website": "Web Hardening Checklist & Hands-On Practice:\n\n1. Essential Nginx Hardening Configuration:\nAdd these production security headers to your web server configuration:\n```nginx\n# Production Defensive Headers\nadd_header Strict-Transport-Security \"max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload\" always;\nadd_header X-Frame-Options \"DENY\" always;\nadd_header X-Content-Type-Options \"nosniff\" always;\nadd_header Referrer-Policy \"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" always;\nadd_header Content-Security-Policy \"default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; object-src 'none';\" always;\nserver_tokens off;\n```\n\n2. Secure Cookie Flags:\nAlways configure session cookies with `Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Strict` to prevent session hijacking via JavaScript.\n\n3. Verify in ABBAY CYBERGUARD M4 Learning Lab:\nAudit target web servers using M4 to inspect SSL/TLS certificates, analyze HTTP security header grades, and generate copy-paste configuration remediation blocks.",
