  "learn.recap.password": "Key Takeaways:\n- Passphrase length provides vastly superior protection compared to short, complex passwords.\n- Never reuse passwords across accounts—one breach must never compromise your entire digital life.\n- App-based Two-Factor Authentication (TOTP) stops 99% of automated credential stuffing attacks.",
  "learn.recap.phishing": "Key Takeaways:\n- Legitimate banks and telecom operators will never request your PIN, password, or OTP via SMS or social messaging.\n- Urgency is the primary psychological weapon of social engineers—always verify through trusted channels before acting.\n- Inspecting link domains before clicking prevents over 90% of credential harvesting attacks.",
  "learn.recap.privacy": "Key Takeaways:\n- What is published online remains permanent and can be harvested by threat actors.\n- Never share unredacted government IDs (Kebele, Fayda) or banking slips on public channels.\n- Always confirm urgent financial requests through an independent voice call before sending money.",
  "learn.recap.response": "Key Takeaways:\n- Rapid containment within the first 15 minutes prevents an incident from turning into catastrophic loss.\n- Always preserve digital evidence (screenshots, headers, transaction IDs) before modifying systems.\n- Never negotiate with extortionists or share confidential passwords in incident reports.",
  "learn.recap.website": "Key Takeaways:\n- HTTPS encrypts traffic in transit, but comprehensive defense requires strict security headers and cookie protections.\n- Never ignore browser certificate warnings—they often signal active eavesdropping or DNS spoofing.\n- Harden web servers by disabling server tokens, enforcing HSTS, and restricting script execution via CSP.",
