  "m1.why.IND-01": "Direct IP connections bypass domain verification and are rarely used by legitimate public consumer services.",
  "m1.why.IND-02": "Browsers ignore userinfo before the @ sign; attackers use this to display trusted names before malicious hosts.",
  "m1.why.IND-03": "Punycode enables homograph attacks where look-alike foreign characters visually mimic familiar brands.",
  "m1.why.IND-04": "Long subdomain chains can push the actual base domain out of view on mobile screens.",
  "m1.why.IND-05": "Unencrypted HTTP connections can be intercepted or altered on public Wi-Fi or compromised routers.",
  "m1.why.IND-06": "Shortened URLs prevent you from evaluating the true landing page before navigating.",
  "m1.why.IND-07": "Deceptive messages frequently simulate account issues or urgent verifications to panic victims.",
  "m1.why.IND-08": "Very long links often embed tracking tokens or obscure look-alike targets within lengthy paths.",
  "m1.why.IND-09": "Excessive percent signs (%xx) mask readable words to evade simple keyword detection.",
  "m1.why.IND-10": "Non-standard port numbers are unusual for consumer websites and can point to personal devices.",
  "m1.why.TXT-01": "Legitimate service providers and banks never request passwords or one-time verification codes via SMS, email, or chat.",
  "m1.why.TXT-02": "Scammers create artificial panic to pressure victims into acting impulsively before verifying claims.",
  "m1.why.TXT-03": "Impersonating trusted Ethiopian institutions (CBE, Telebirr, Ethio telecom) is the most common social engineering tactic.",
  "m1.why.TXT-04": "Advance-fee fraud lures victims with fake prizes or awards to convince them to provide personal information or money.",
  "m1.why.TXT-05": "Scammers require an upfront transfer under the pretext of delivery or verification fees before absconding.",
  "m1.why.TXT-06": "Phishing messages often embed deceptive or shortened links to redirect users to credential-harvesting pages.",
  "m1.why.TXT-07": "Directing users to private messaging channels or sideloaded APK files bypasses platform security and installs spyware.",
  "m1.why.TXT-08": "Official organizations and banks send communications from their own registered domains, not free accounts like Gmail or Yahoo.",
  "m1.why.TXT-09": "Unsolicited requests for bank account numbers and financial details are frequently used to initiate unauthorized transfers, impersonate account holders, or execute fake payout scams.",
  "m1.why.TXT-10": "Collecting identity attributes (such as full name, age, gender, occupation, or ID numbers) allows fraudsters to build social engineering profiles or attempt unauthorized SIM swaps and account takeovers.",
  "m1.why_label": "Why it matters",
