  "m4.desc": "M4 is an educational scenario explorer that demonstrates defensive security findings using bundled simulations rather than live scanning. It does not accept custom URLs or contact external websites.",
  "m4.distinction": "Looking to inspect a link you received? Use M1 Link Checker to analyze URL text. M4 is strictly for learning how website defenses are configured.",
  "m4.exp.CHK-01": "A valid certificate lets browsers verify the site. Defense: renew certificates before expiry and automate renewal.",
  "m4.exp.CHK-02": "Plain-HTTP visitors should be sent to HTTPS. Defense: redirect all HTTP traffic to HTTPS.",
  "m4.exp.CHK-03": "HSTS tells browsers to always use HTTPS. Defense: send the header with a suitable max-age.",
  "m4.exp.CHK-04": "CSP limits where scripts can load from and reduces script-injection impact. Defense: define a restrictive policy.",
  "m4.exp.CHK-05": "Headers such as X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy and Permissions-Policy add protection. Defense: set each deliberately.",
  "m4.exp.CHK-06": "Secure, HttpOnly and SameSite flags protect session cookies. Defense: set all three.",
  "m4.exp.CHK-07": "Server or X-Powered-By values reveal software versions. Defense: remove or minimise them.",
  "m4.fix": "What to do",
  "m4.instruction": "Select DS-A, DS-B, or DS-C below to explore simulated findings for TLS certificates, HTTPS redirects, HSTS, CSP, security headers, cookie attributes, and version disclosure.",
  "m4.mode": "Mode: DEMO (simulated, offline). Live mode is not available in this release.",
  "m4.pick": "Choose a simulated example",
  "m4.result": "SIMULATED RESULT — not an actual scan",
  "m4.scope": "These findings are bundled test data and cover a small set of settings. They say nothing about any real website, and passing checks never mean a site is secure.",
  "m4.st.missing": "Missing (simulated)",
  "m4.st.present": "Present (simulated)",
  "m4.st.unknown": "Could not determine (simulated)",
